    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d87">

                <pb facs="0094" n="84" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg84"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/967: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-11T11:00:00-06:00">December 11, 1941—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>390. The President has just informed me that he is only awaiting official word
                    from me that a state of war exists between the United States and Germany and
                    Italy to issue a decree declaring war against Italy and Germany.<anchor n="43"
                        xml:id="d87-f1"/> He said he will also take steps similar to those outlined
                    in the Department’s circular telegram of the 10th.<anchor n="44" xml:id="d87-f2"
                    /></p>
                <p>I would appreciate receiving Department’s suggestion as to whether German and
                    Italian diplomatic representatives should leave Costa Rica via the Canal Zone or
                    otherwise. President said he would be guided by our views.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lane</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d87-f1" n="43" xml:id="d87-f1-content">
                <p>President Rafael Calderón Guardia of Costa Rica on December 11, 1941, signed the
                    decree declaring a state of war between Costa Rica and Germany and Italy.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d87-f2" n="44" xml:id="d87-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; this telegram outlined steps which had been taken to control alien
                    enemies in the United States (740.00115 European War/1617a).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
